# ── credentials ──
# A .p8 is an App Store Connect private key: whoever holds it can act on the
# developer account, and Apple only issues it once. It belongs on the machine
# and in a password manager, never in the tree. These patterns are a backstop
# for a stray `git add -A`, not the actual protection.
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
AuthKey_*
.appstoreconnect/
private_keys/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── build output ──
node_modules/
ios/
android/
*.ipa
*.xcarchive
*.dSYM

# ── scratch ──
*.log
*.done
chunks/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# local secrets — never commit
.secrets/
